 solar technology and manufacturing company. The only U.S.-headquartered company among the world's largest solar manufacturers, First Solar is focused on competitively and reliably enabling power generation needs with our advanced, uniquely American thin film PV technology. Developed at R&D labs in California and Ohio, our technology provides a competitive, high-performance, and responsibly produced alternative to conventional crystalline silicon PV solar modules. Our PV solar modules are produced using a fully integrated, continuous process that does not rely on Chinese crystalline silicon supply chains.","zh":"我們是美國領先的光伏太陽能技術和製造公司。作為世界上最大的太陽能製造商中唯一一家總部位於美國的公司，First Solar 致力於透過我們先進、獨特的美國薄膜光伏技術，以具有競爭力且可靠的方式滿足發電需求。我們的技術由加州和俄亥俄州的研發實驗室開發，為傳統晶體矽光伏太陽能模組提供了具有競爭力、高性能且負責任生產的替代品。我們的光伏太陽能模組採用完全整合的連續流程生產，不依賴中國晶體矽供應鏈。"},{"en":"We are the world's largest thin film PV solar module manufacturer and the largest PV solar module manufacturer in the Western Hemisphere. In addressing the overall global demand for electricity, PV solar modules provide energy at a lower levelized cost of electricity (\"LCOE\"), meaning the net present value of a system's total life cycle costs divided by the quantity of energy that is expected to be produced over the system's life, when compared to traditional forms of energy generation. With over $2 billion in cumulative R&D investments in the last 20 years, we have a demonstrated history of innovation and continuous improvement. We believe our strategies and points of differentiation provide the foundation for our competitive position and enable us to remain one of the preferred providers of PV solar modules.","zh":"我們是全球最大的薄膜光伏太陽能組件製造商和西半球最大的光伏太陽能組件製造商。在滿足全球整體電力需求時，光電太陽能模組以較低的平準電力成本（「LCOE」）提供能源，這意味著與傳統形式的能源發電相比，系統總生命週期成本的淨現值除以系統生命週期內預計產生的能源量。過去 20 年來，我們累計研發投資超過 20 億美元，擁有悠久的創新和持續改進歷史。我們相信，我們的策略和差異化點為我們的競爭地位奠定了基礎，並使我們能夠繼續成為光伏太陽能組件的首選供應商之一。"},{"en":"Our current module semiconductor structure is a single-junction polycrystalline thin film that uses CdTe as the absorption layer. CdTe has absorption properties that are well matched to the solar spectrum and can deliver competitive performance using approximately 2% to 3% of the amount of semiconductor material used to manufacture conventional crystalline silicon modules. In terms of performance, in many climates our solar modules provide certain energy production advantages relative to competing crystalline silicon modules. For example, our CdTe solar technology provides:","zh":"我們目前的模組半導體結構是單接面多晶薄膜，使用CdTe作為吸收層。 CdTe 具有與太陽光譜非常匹配的吸收特性，並且使用用於製造傳統晶體矽模組的半導體材料量的約 2% 至 3% 即可提供具有競爭力的性能。就性能而言，在許多氣候條件下，我們的太陽能組件相對於競爭對手的晶體矽組件具有一定的能源生產優勢。例如，我們的 CdTe 太陽能技術提供："}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Our customers include system developers, independent power producers, utilities, commercial and industrial companies, large corporate energy buyers, and other system owners and operators. During 2025, we sold the majority of our solar modules to customers with projects in the United States. During 2025, Silicon Ranch Corporation and NextEra Energy each accounted for 10% or more of our modules business net sales. For more information about risks related to our customers, see Item 1A. \"Risk Factors – The loss of any of our large customers, or the inability of our customers and counterparties to perform under their contracts with us, including through terminations by customers of any contract in part or in full, has reduced and, in the future, could significantly reduce our net sales and negatively impact our results of operations.\"","zh":"我們的客戶包括系統開發商、獨立電力生產商、公用事業公司、商業和工業公司、大型企業能源買家以及其他系統所有者和營運商。 2025年，我們將大部分太陽能模組出售給在美國有專案的客戶。 2025年，Silicon Ranch Corporation和NextEra Energy分別占我們組件業務淨銷售額的10%或以上。有關與我們的客戶相關的風險的更多資訊，請參閱第 1A 項。 “風險因素——我們失去任何大客戶，或者我們的客戶和交易對手無法履行與我們簽訂的合同，包括客戶部分或全部終止任何合同，已經減少了，並且在未來可能會顯著減少我們的淨銷售額，並對我們的經營業績產生負面影響。”"},{"en":"We continue to focus on certain key geographic markets, particularly in areas with abundant solar resources, durable electricity load growth, and a diverse set of customers. Regulated utilities continue to invest in utility scale solar to meet growing electricity demand, replace retiring generation assets, manage long term power costs, and support system reliability, often through utility owned projects or long term power purchase agreements. Corporate buyers—particularly technology, data infrastructure, manufacturing, and logistics companies with significant electricity requirements—are increasingly active participants in the market, primarily through long term offtake arrangements designed to secure large volumes of electricity from utility scale solar projects. Independent power producers and infrastructure oriented investors play a central role in developing, owning, and financing th","zh":"我們繼續專注於某些關鍵地理市場，特別是太陽能資源豐富、電力負載持續成長和客戶多元化的地區。受監管的公用事業公司通常透過公用事業公司擁有的專案或長期購電協議，繼續投資公用事業規模的太陽能，以滿足不斷增長的電力需求，更換退役的發電資產，管理長期電力成本並支持系統可靠性。企業買家，特別是具有大量電力需求的技術、數據基礎設施、製造和物流公司，越來越積極參與市場，主要透過長期承購安排來確保公用事業規模太陽能專案的大量電力。獨立電力生產商和基礎設施導向投資者在開發、擁有和融資方面發揮核心作用"}],"competition":[{"en":"The solar energy and renewable energy sectors are highly competitive and continually evolving as participants in these sectors strive to distinguish themselves within their markets and compete within the larger electric power industry. Among PV solar module manufacturers, the principal method of competition is sales price per watt, which may be influenced by several module value attributes, including wattage (through a larger form factor or an improved conversion efficiency), energy yield, degradation, sustainability, and reliability. Sales price per watt may also be influenced by warranty terms, customer payment terms, and/or module attributes. We face intense competition for sales of solar modules, which may result in reduced selling prices and loss of market share. Our primary source of competition is crystalline silicon module manufacturers, the majority of which are linked to China.","zh":"太陽能和再生能源行業競爭激烈，並且不斷發展，因為這些行業的參與者努力在其市場中脫穎而出並在更大的電力行業中競爭。在光伏太陽能組件製造商中，競爭的主要方式是每瓦的銷售價格，這可能受到組件價值屬性的影響，包括瓦數（透過更大的外形尺寸或提高的轉換效率）、能源產量、退化、永續性和可靠性。每瓦銷售價格也可能受到保固條款、客戶付款條款和/或模組屬性的影響。我們面臨太陽能組件銷售的激烈競爭，這可能導致銷售價格下降和市場份額喪失。我們主要的競爭來源是晶體矽組件製造商，其中大部分與中國有關。"},{"en":"We also expect to compete with future entrants into the PV solar industry and existing market participants that offer new or differentiated technological solutions. For additional information, see Item 1A. \"Risk Factors – Our failure to further refine our technology and develop and introduce improved PV products, including as a result of delays in implementing planned advancements, could render our solar modules uncompetitive and reduce our net sales, profitability, and/or market share.\"","zh":"我們還期望與光伏太陽能行業的未來進入者以及提供新的或差異化技術解決方案的現有市場參與者競爭。有關更多資訊，請參閱第 1A 項。 “風險因素——我們未能進一步完善我們的技術以及開發和推出改進的光伏產品，包括由於延遲實施計劃的進步而導致的結果，可能會使我們的太陽能組件失去競爭力，並減少我們的淨銷售額、盈利能力和/或市場份額。”"}],"segments":{"geo":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"US","val":4994679000,"zh":"美國"},{"name":"IN","val":195584000,"zh":"印度"},{"name":"Allotherforeigncountries","val":22810000,"zh":"所有其他國家"},{"name":"FR","val":6303000,"zh":"FR"}],"total":5219376000}},"peers":["SPWR","CSIQ","ENPH","SEDG","RUN"]}}